Court procedure at initial appearance. 

(a) The judge shall inform the defendant of: 
(1) the charge or charges against him; 
(2) the maximum penalty allowed under Tribal Law for the offense; 
(3) the defendant's right to counsel provided by the Defense Advocate's office or to 
obtain private counsel at his own expense; 
(4) the right to call any witness on his behalf; 
(5) the right to request a jury trial; 
(6) the right to remain silent and that any statement made by him may be used in 
evidence against him at any subsequent court proceedings; 
(7) the general circumstances under which the defendant may obtain pretrial 
release; 
(8) the right to cross examine the Colony's witnesses; and 
(9) the right to have up to 10 working days before arraignment. 

(b) The judge may admit the defendant to bail as provided herein.

Criteria for determining bail and conditions of release. 

(a) The criteria for determining the amount of bail and conditions of release include, but are 
not limited to the following: 
(1) defendant's employment status and work history; 
(2) defendant's financial condition; 
(3) the nature and extent of defendant's family relationships 
(4) defendant's ties to the Reno-Sparks Indian Colony community; 
(5) defendant's past and present residences; 
(6) names of individuals personally agreeing to assure defendant's court appearances; 
(7) the nature and circumstances of the current charge, including whether the offense 
involved the use of force or violence; 
(8) the defendant's prior criminal record, if any, and whether, at the time of the 
current arrest or offense, the defendant was on probation, on parole, or on other release pending trial, 
sentencing, or appeal for an offense; 

