(9) the defendant's record of appearance at court proceedings; and 
(10) the nature and seriousness of the danger to any person or the community that 
would be posed by the defendant's release; and 
(11) any other information relating to the likelihood of defendant appearing at all 
appropriate times.

Sentencing considerations. 

(a) Before imposing sentence, the Tribal Judge shall consider the following: 
(1) the nature of the crime committed; 
(2) the circumstances under which the crime was committed; 
(3) the prospects of rehabilitation of the offender; 
(4) the possible resources and needs of the offender's dependents, if any; 
(5) the criminal history of the offender; 
(6) alternatives to imprisonment of the offender; 
(7) the ability of the defendant to pay a fine; and 
(8) whether the defendant suffers from a mental illness 


